RF.put("questb:b24",{"8664":{"id":8664,"t":"Doomcaller's Mantle","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 6,600 experience instead of 9,950, 0.66 times as much.","obj":"Bring the Qiraji Bindings of Dominance, 2 Idols of the Sage, 5 Bronze Scarabs and 5 Bone Scarabs to Andorgos in Ahn'Qiraj. You must also attain Neutral reputation with the Brood of Nozdormu to complete this quest.\nQiraji Bindings of Dominance Viscidus in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Princess Huhuran in Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n2 Idol of the Sage Vekniss Soldier 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Stinger 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Bronze Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Bone Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\nReach 0 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","desc":"It is said among us that the ornate shoulder armor worn by the mortal races started as an attempt to emulate the wings of a dragon.\nBring me the bindings worn by the highest Qiraji leaders and I shall shape them into a set of pauldrons more dreadful than even the wings of Nefarian himself!","rew":"You will receive:\nDoomcaller's Mantle\nExperience: 6,600\n+200 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","back":"Have you collected the components I require?","done":"From the materials you bring and from the scales of our fallen Qiraji foes I make you these pauldrons, mortal. May they grant you the protection you need and may the sight of them strike fear into our enemies.\nStart Andorgos Ahn'Qiraj Temple End Andorgos Ahn'Qiraj Temple Level 60 , requires level 60 Difficulty 60 Side Both factions Class Warlock Type Raid Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 8664\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 60, 13,200 XP in all.\n1 [ 60 ] Mortal Champions\nKandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n6,600 XP\n2 [ 60 ] Doomcaller's Mantle this quest\nBring the Qiraji Bindings of Dominance, 2 Idols of the Sage, 5 Bronze Scarabs and 5 Bone Scarabs to Andorgos in Ahn'Qiraj.\nAndorgos Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n6,600 XP","cats":["ahnqiraj"]},"8504":{"id":8504,"t":"The Alliance Needs More Stranglekelp!","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 20 stranglekelp to Private Draxlegauge at the airfield in Dun Morogh.\n20 Stranglekelp Stranglekelp , Apothecary Quinard 61.5 % , General Kirika 61.5 % , Marshal Bluewall 61.5 % and 4 more","desc":"Well hello again there... what was it? Ah yes, ‹name›! Come to see if I still need more stranglekelp have you? Well, it's your lucky day, because the answer to that very important question is a very affirmative YES! Think you could gather up twenty more?","rew":"You will receive:\n3 Alliance Commendation Signet Ahn'Qiraj War Effort Supplies","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.5,"y":32.7,"n":"Private Draxlegauge","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj-war"]},"504":{"id":504,"t":"Crushridge Warmongers","lv":40,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. New rewards: Alterac Assassin's Gloves.","obj":"Slay 10 Crushridge Warmongers, then return to Marshal Redpath in Southshore.\nCrushridge Warmonger slain : 0/ 10","desc":"Now that you've had a taste of the Crushridge ogres, I want you to really bloody their noses...\nGo into the Ruins of Alterac and seek out the Crushridge Warmongers. I want you to cut down a good number of them - that's the only way those brutes will learn to keep their distance from Alliance territory.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nBurning Sliver Lunar Buckler Alterac Assassin's Gloves\nNew in Forever: Alterac Assassin's Gloves.\nExperience: 4,700\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"You have more Warmongers to slay, ‹name›. You should be up on the mountains on your task, not down here with your weapon stowed.","done":"Very good. Here is your reward.\nAnd when you were hunting those Warmongers, how did Alterac city look? It's in bad shape I would guess. Ogres are not known for their cleanliness.\nThankfully, your efforts will help keep them away from Southshore.\nHillsbrad Foothills Alterac Mountains","pins":[{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":49.5,"y":58.7,"n":"Marshal Redpath","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["alterac-mountains"]},"7224":{"id":7224,"t":"Enemy Booty","lv":60,"min":51,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 20 Armor Scraps to Smith Regzar in Frostwolf Village.\n20 Armor Scraps Winterax Warrior 80 % , Winterax Mystic 80 % , Corporal Teeka Bloodsnarl 80 % , Alliance Sentinel 80 % and 4 more","desc":"When you fight the enemy, gather the scraps of their armor and bring them to me. I'll use those scraps to make armor for our own troops!","rew":"Experience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Frostwolf Clan\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"How goes the hunting, ‹name›. Do you have any armor scraps for me?","done":"These will do nicely. I'll melt them down and patch them up and you'll never know they came from those Stormpike cowards!\nThanks, ‹name›. And let me polish up that armor of yours...\nStart Smith Regzar Alterac Valley End Smith Regzar Alterac Valley Level 60 , requires level 51 Difficulty 51 56 58 Side Horde Type PvP Shareable Yes Quest ID 7224\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 60, 6,600 XP in all.\n1 [ 60 ] Enemy Booty this quest\nBring 20 Armor Scraps to Smith Regzar in Frostwolf Village.\nSmith Regzar Alterac Valley\n6,600 XP\n2 [ 60 ] More Booty!\nSmith Regzar Alterac Valley","cats":["alterac-valley"]},"8264":{"id":8264,"t":"Defiler's Standard Care Package","lv":44,"min":35,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nDefiler's Standard Care Package\nExperience: 380\n+10 reputation with The Defilers","done":"You've certainly begun to prove yourself to us, ‹name›. As a reward, please take this care package! Inside it you'll find rations and bandages that are usable only inside Arathi Basin.\nAs you continue to prove yourself inside the Basin, you'll find that these items will become available to you for purchase. Rations become available when you are Honored with us, and bandages when you are Revered.","pins":[{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":73.4,"y":29.7,"n":"Rutherford Twing","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["arathi-basin"]},"664":{"id":664,"t":"Drowned Sorrows","lv":40,"min":35,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Captain Steelgut in Faldir's Cove wants you to kill 10 Daggerspine Raiders and 3 Daggerspine Sorceresses.\nDaggerspine Raider slain : 0/ 10\nDaggerspine Sorceress slain : 0/ 3","desc":"Argh, 'tis a horrible life. I should be in a watery grave right now, not sittin' here by the fire, breathin' fresh air.\nThe crew tried so hard to save my beautiful Maiden's Folly. Bless the boys, bless their hearts.\nO'Breen made it to shore safely but we weren't so lucky. The seas just sank on us, I swear.\nOne second we're afloat and the next water is rushin' in. And those beasts! Killed all the survivors. Horrible naga scum. I went black and ended up here, saved.\nI want those beasts dead.","rew":"You will receive:\nSeawolf Gloves\nExperience: 3,150\n+100 reputation with Booty Bay\n-500 reputation with Bloodsail Buccaneers","back":"Bah, maybe I should go kill those naga scum myself. It's obvious you're not goin' to do it.\nMaybe I can find some knitting needles so you can keep yourself busy.","done":"Nice work out there, ‹name›.\nThose scum deserved what they got. While nothin' will ever bring me ship or me crew back, the death of those naga gives me some solace.","pins":[{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":34,"y":80.8,"n":"Captain Steelgut","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["arathi-highlands"]},"824":{"id":824,"t":"Je'neu of the Earthen Ring","lv":27,"min":23,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Befouled Water Globe to Je'neu Sancrea at Zoram'gar Outpost, Ashenvale.\nBefouled Water Globe Tideress\nProvided: Befouled Water Globe","desc":"The Earthen Ring is a shamanistic group dedicated to studying and preserving the elements. They have forgotten more about crazy old gods, ancient legends and lore than most scholars will ever know.\nLucky for you, I know someone in the Earthen Ring here in Ashenvale. Head over to Zoram'gar Outpost on the coast of the Zoram Strand; show Je'neu Sancrea what you found. If anyone can figure out that globe's significance, it'd be him.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nDeftkin Belt Driftmire Shield Soft Willow Cape\nExperience: 2,200\n+100 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"Ah, hello there. I spend a great deal of time studying the water - all the elements really - so much so that sometimes I don't even notice people around me.\nIs there something I can help you with?","done":"This globe... it is most disturbing. Many of the more powerful elementals receive their power and energy through such devices. To find one like this nearly intact is one thing - to find it so tainted is another.\nI will see that this globe is studied properly by the Earthen Ring. Perhaps we can bring an end to this corruption of the elements. Please - accept this as a fair exchange for bringing this globe to the attention of the Earthen Ring.","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":73.7,"y":60,"n":"Mastok Wrilehiss","s":1},{"z":"Ashenvale","x":11.6,"y":34.3,"n":"Je'neu Sancrea","e":1}],"cats":["ashenvale"]},"24":{"id":24,"t":"Shadumbra's Head","lv":27,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Shadumbra's Head to Senani Thunderheart at Splintertree Post, Ashenvale.\nShadumbra's Head Shadumbra\nProvided: Shadumbra's Head","desc":"The once swift Shadumbra now lies still as you claim victory over it. The head of the slain nightsaber is a fitting trophy for this fight of the Ashenvale Hunt. Senani Thunderheart at Splintertree Post will want to see such a trophy to award you credit for this part of the Ashenvale Hunt.","rew":"Experience: 2,200\n+100 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"Greetings once again, ‹name›! Have you come to show me proof of your hunt?","done":"A victory for ‹name› in the Ashenvale Hunt! Well done - the head of Shadumbra is a fitting trophy to claim for such an impressive fight, no doubt.\nShadumbra's savagery was well known throughout the post here. Any trip to the west, especially on foot trying to get out to the Zoram Strand, was wrought with danger because of this tiger. Thanks to you, this danger has abated.","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":73.8,"y":61.5,"n":"Senani Thunderheart","e":1}],"cats":["ashenvale"]},"6504":{"id":6504,"t":"The Lost Pages","lv":30,"min":23,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find the 12 missing pages of the Shredder Operating Manual, and put them together to form Chapters 1, 2, and 3. Return the pages to Gurda Ragescar near Splintertree Post.\nShredder Operating Manual - Chapter 1\nShredder Operating Manual - Chapter 2\nShredder Operating Manual - Chapter 3","desc":"I just picked up this shredder from Ratchet and I was on my way back to the Warsong Lumber Camp, where I am supposed to be on duty. I was given a manual on how to operate the shredder, but on the trip back, a huge gust of wind blew it from my hands. The pages went everywhere, and all I was left with was the cover.\nThe pages could be just about anywhere by now, I suppose... but I don't know how to use the shredder without them! Will you find them for me?","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nShredder Operating Gloves Oilrag Handwraps\nExperience: 3,650\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"I hope you find the pages soon, ‹name›! I really need to get back to work!","done":"Reading isn't my strong point... but now I'll be able to get back to work! Thanks, ‹name›!","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":70,"y":71.2,"n":"Gurda Ragescar","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ashenvale"]},"7864":{"id":7864,"t":"Sentinel Standard Care Package","lv":44,"min":35,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nSentinel Standard Care Package\nExperience: 380\n+10 reputation with Silverwing Sentinels","done":"You've certainly begun to prove yourself to us, ‹name›. As a reward, please take this care package! Inside it you'll find rations and bandages that are usable only inside Warsong Gulch.\nAs you continue to prove yourself inside the Gulch, you'll find that these items will become available to you for purchase. Rations become available when you are Friendly with us, and bandages when you are Honored.","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":61.5,"y":83.9,"n":"Illiyana Moonblaze","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ashenvale"]},"6824":{"id":6824,"t":"Hands of the Enemy","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 55 instead of 60.","obj":"Bring the Hands of Lucifron, Sulfuron, Gehennas and Shazzrah to Duke Hydraxis in Azshara.\nHand of Shazzrah Shazzrah\nHand of Lucifron Lucifron\nHand of Gehennas Gehennas\nHand of Sulfuron Sulfuron Harbinger","desc":"‹name›, your service is of great value to us, so we are reluctant to send you on this last mission for we do not want to lose such a useful agent.\nBut its success would further our war efforts tremendously and... it was deemed worth risking you.\nWe want these captains in the Molten Core destroyed: Lucifron, Sulfuron, Gehennas and Shazzrah. Kill them and bring me their hands!\nThis task will take every resource you possess, ‹name›, but if you can do it then the Firelords will be dealt a terrible blow.","rew":"Experience: 9,950","back":"Have you defeated Lucifron and the others, ‹name›? Do you have the hands of the enemy?","done":"You have the hands! You defeated the fire captains! I would not have thought it possible, had I not known you and what you are capable of.\n‹name›, your exploits are without number, but word of this last feat will send waves among the Waterlords. Your name may one day be legend to us.\nSpeak with me again, ‹name›. I may have yet another task...","pins":[{"z":"Azshara","x":79.3,"y":73.7,"n":"Duke Hydraxis","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["azshara"]},"4264":{"id":4264,"t":"A Crumpled Up Note","lv":58,"min":50,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"You may have just stumbled on to something that Marshal Windsor would be interested in seeing. There may be hope, after all.\nA Crumpled Up Note Jaz 25 % , Crest Killer 25 % , Shill Dinger 25 % , Ograbisi 25 % and 4 more\nProvided: A Crumpled Up Note","desc":"The note has stains covering its surface. The text is barely legible, but you make out the following:\n...sweet irony...\n...the fall of the broken Alliance...\n...if it were not for General Angerforge's diligence, we may have never discovered the pattern to the encryption...\n...Argelmach is almost done with the decryption of Windsor's notes.\nOur lord will rise from the depths and crush any that remain...\n-Emperor Dagran Thaurissan.","rew":"Experience: 6,200\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"<Marshal Windsor eyes the note in your hand.>\nWhat do you have there, ‹name›?","done":"<Marshal Windsor takes the note and begins reading.>\nStart an item: A Crumpled Up Note End Marshal Windsor Level 58 , requires level 50 Difficulty 50 54 56 Side Alliance Type Dungeon Shareable No Quest ID 4264\nThe chain\n16 quests from level 54 to 60, 77,300 XP in all.\n1 [ 54 ] Dragonkin Menace\nSlay 15 Black Broodlings, 10 Black Dragonspawn, 4 Black Wyrmkin and 1 Black Drake.\nHelendis Riverhorn Burning Steppes\n5,450 XP\n2 [ 54 ] The True Masters\nTravel to Lakeshire and deliver Helendis Riverhorn's Letter to Magistrate Solomon.\nHelendis Riverhorn Burning Steppes\n4,100 XP\n3 [ 54 ] The True Masters\nTravel to Stormwind and deliver Solomon's Plea to Highlord Bolvar Fordragon. Bolvar resides in Stormwind Keep.\nMagistrate Solomon Redridge Mountains\n4,100 XP\n4 [ 54 ] The True Masters\nSpeak with Highlord Bolvar Fordragon after speaking with Lady Katrana Prestor.\nHighlord Bolvar Fordragon Stormwind City\n550 XP\n5 [ 54 ] The True Masters\nTake Bolvar's Decree to Magistrate Solomon in Lakeshire.\nHighlord Bolvar Fordragon Stormwind City\n5,450 XP\n6 [ 54 ] The True Masters\nSpeak with Marshal Maxwell in the Burning Steppes.\nMagistrate Solomon Redridge Mountains\n550 XP\n7 [ 54 ] The True Masters\nSpeak with Ragged John to learn of Marshal Windsor's fate and return to Marshal Maxwell when you have completed this task. You recall Marshal Maxwell telling you to search for h\nMarshal Maxwell Burning Steppes\n550 XP\n8 [ 54 ] Marshal Windsor\nTravel to Blackrock Mountain in the northwest and enter Blackrock Depths.\nMarshal Maxwell Burning Steppes\n5,450 XP\n9 [ 54 ] Abandoned Hope\nGive Marshal Maxwell the bad news.\nMarshal Windsor\n5,450 XP\n10 [ 58 ] A Crumpled Up Note this quest\nYou may have just stumbled on to something that Marshal Windsor would be interested in seeing.\nA Crumpled Up Note\n6,200 XP\n11 [ 58 ] A Shred of Hope\nReturn Marshal Windsor's Lost Information. Marshal Windsor believes that the information is being held by Golem Lord Argelmach and General Angerforge.\nMarshal Windsor\n6,200 XP\n12 [ 58 ] Jail Break!\nHelp Marshal Windsor get his gear back and free his friends.\nMarshal Windsor\n7,750 XP\n13 [ 60 ] Stormwind Rendezvous\nTravel to Stormwind City and venture to the city gates.\nMarsha","cats":["blackrock-depths"]},"4024":{"id":4024,"t":"A Taste of Flame","lv":58,"min":52,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to Blackrock Depths and slay Bael'Gar.\nYou only know that the giant resides inside Blackrock Depths. Remember to use the Altered Black Dragonflight Molt on Bael'Gar's remains to capture the Fiery Essence.\nReturn the Encased Fiery Essence to Cyrus Therepentous.\nEncased Fiery Essence\nProvided: Altered Black Dragonflight Molt","desc":"I wish to taste the searing flames of the mountain of fire. To let the molten fires of Blackrock cascade across my being. That essence, that searing heat, it is what I crave.\nBael'Gar resides in the Depths of Blackrock: A being of pure flame, born of the fires of Ragnaros. Slay Bael'Gar and from his smoldering remains bring for me a piece of his inner fire.\nUse the molt on his remains to safely extract the inner flame.\nSucceed and be rewarded.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nShaleskin Cape Wyrmhide Spaulders Valconian Sash\nMoney: 2 65 2 gold, 65 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,200","back":"Has the giant been felled?","done":"<Cyrus snatches the fiery essence from your hands.>\nYES!\nTake your prize and be gone. Leave my sight at once!","pins":[{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":95.1,"y":31.6,"n":"Cyrus Therepentous","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blackrock-depths"]},"2584":{"id":2584,"t":"Spirit of the Boar","lv":50,"min":45,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring three Blasted Boar Lungs, two Scorpok Pincers, and one Basilisk Brain to Bloodmage Drazial.\n3 Blasted Boar Lung Ashmane Boar 40 % , Helboar 40 % , Grunter 30 %\n2 Scorpok Pincer Scorpok Stinger 40 % , Clack the Reaver 30 %\nBasilisk Brain Redstone Basilisk 40 % , Redstone Crystalhide 40 % , Deatheye 30 %","desc":"When I first administered the elixir, ‹name›, I could tell that one or two applications would not satiate your appetite. Even now, I can see the hunger in your eyes. The concoction has addictive properties of which, seemingly, the most strong of will cannot resist.\nSo be it! Should you require more of the lung juice cocktail, venture back into the wasteland and find for me three blasted boar lungs, two scorpok pincers, and one basilisk brain.","rew":"You will receive:\nLung Juice Cocktail","back":"Where are the organs, ‹name›!?","done":"I must warn you, ‹name›, do not attempt to mix the formulas I have created. The chemical properties of the formula you most recently ingested will always take precedence over former enchantments; thus, rendering the other formulation null.","pins":[{"z":"Blasted Lands","x":50.6,"y":14.2,"n":"Bloodmage Drazial","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blasted-lands"]},"2744":{"id":2744,"t":"The Demon Hunter","lv":60,"min":45,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Loramus Thalipedes in Azshara.","desc":"The triad is protected by Razelikh.\nIn exchange for their servitude, Razelikh granted each of them nearly unlimited power within the Blasted Lands. The amulet pieces are each attuned to the lifeforce of their owner, granting them immortality. As long as they remain within the Blasted Lands, they cannot be slain, their life spans extended until the end of days.\nThere is one who may be able to assist you further, ‹name›. Travel to Azshara and find the demon hunter, Loramus Thalipedes. Search the islands.","rew":"Experience: 6,600","back":"What are you doing here?","done":"I will help you. Although, I do not think you fully understand what you are up against.\nSwamp of Sorrows Azshara","pins":[{"z":"Swamp of Sorrows","x":34.3,"y":66.1,"n":"Fallen Hero of the Horde","s":1},{"z":"Azshara","x":60.8,"y":66.4,"n":"Loramus Thalipedes","e":1}],"cats":["blasted-lands"]},"4184":{"id":4184,"t":"The True Masters","lv":54,"min":48,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to Stormwind and deliver Solomon's Plea to Highlord Bolvar Fordragon.\nBolvar resides in Stormwind Keep.\nSolomon's Plea to Bolvar\nProvided: Solomon's Plea to Bolvar","desc":"This is grim news, ‹name›. To discover that our mortal enemies are merely pawns of a much greater threat is disheartening. There is no possible way that Lakeshire could survive an attack from both the Blackrock orcs and the black dragonflight. Should Lakeshire fall to this menace, Darkshire would fall next, and then what? Goldshire? Stormwind itself?\nYou must take this information to Highlord Bolvar Fordragon in Stormwind at once! If this does not merit the aid of Stormwind, nothing will and all is lost.","rew":"Experience: 4,100\n+75 reputation with Stormwind","back":"What brings you to Stormwind Keep?","done":"Dragons? Impossible!\nRedridge Mountains Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Redridge Mountains","x":24.9,"y":44.5,"n":"Magistrate Solomon","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":80.2,"y":38.3,"n":"Highlord Bolvar Fordragon","e":1}],"cats":["burning-steppes"]},"97944":{"id":97944,"t":"Camping 101 herbalism","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Malorne Bladeleaf in Dolanaar to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.\nRaise your herbalism skill to 20","desc":"Looks to me like you've gained some skill in herbalism. Picking flowers isn't just for dilly-dallying, you know. It can be useful... and profitable.\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft an Incense Candle for your camp. High spirits are a key component to keeping healers and spellcasters in the fight, and an Incense Candle can provide a boost that magic users will surely appreciate.","done":"There you have it, you can now craft your very own Incense Candle. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics.","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":57.6,"y":56.6,"n":"Lyreena Duskblade","s":1},{"z":"Teldrassil","x":57.6,"y":60.6,"n":"Malorne Bladeleaf","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"96984":{"id":96984,"t":"Heart of disruption","lv":33,"min":24,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Collect the Arcane Mote in the City of Dalaran for Magus Wordeen Voidglare in Tarren Mill.\nArcane Mote","desc":"You may not have our best interests at heart, but I won't deny an extra pair of hands. And if Dalaran falls, it takes everything with it--including your Undercity.\nSo, your benefactor wants in? Fine. I'll imbue your key to work past my wards so you can enter the city. Once you're in, meet me at the Violet Citadel where this all began. With everything going on the Kirin Tor will be too busy to stop you.\nScavenge what you will, but whatever happens, our first priority is to prevent a catastrophe.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nBattle Spaulders Enchanted Sandals Striking Staff\nExperience: 9,400","pins":[{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":68.6,"y":45.2,"n":"Image of Archmage Modera","s":1}],"cats":["city-of-dalaran"]},"94344":{"id":94344,"t":"Craftsmans writ gordok ogre suit","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Gordok Ogre Suit\nGordok Ogre Suit","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Gordok Ogre Suit, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Gordok Ogre Suit Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94344","cats":["crafting"]},"94264":{"id":94264,"t":"Craftsmans writ shadow oil","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Shadow Oil\nShadow Oil","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Shadow Oil, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Shadow Oil Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94264","cats":["crafting"]},"7944":{"id":7944,"t":"Your Fortune Awaits You...","lv":60,"min":10,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to the Wailing Caverns in the Barrens and seek out your fortune.\nSayge's Fortune #25\nProvided: Sayge's Fortune #25","desc":"\"Your fortune awaits you inside Wailing Caverns.\"\nThe fortune Sayge handed you feels slightly warm to the touch. Grasping it firmly, you see an image of a cave to the southwest of the Crossroads in the Barrens. Focusing closer in on the image, you wind about twisty passages until you reach a shimmering portal... one that leads into the heart of the caverns itself. Stepping through it, a strange chest appears out from nowhere.","rew":"You will receive:\nMysterious Lockbox\nExperience: 650\n+50 reputation with Darkmoon Faire","back":"This chest looks like the one from your vision...","done":"A quick search of the chest reveals a lockbox from within it! It would seem that you have found your fortune!\nStart an item: Sayge's Fortune #25 End Mysterious Wailing Caverns Chest Level 60 , requires level 10 Difficulty 10 56 58 Side Human, Orc, Dwarf, Night Elf, Undead, Tauren, Gnome, Troll Shareable No Repeatable Yes Quest ID 7944","cats":["darkmoon-faire"]},"984":{"id":984,"t":"How Big a Threat?","lv":14,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find a corrupt furbolg camp in Darkshore and return to Terenthis in Auberdine.\nFind the place the quest sends you to.","desc":"Some of my brethren were rescued from a corrupt furbolg in Teldrassil, and I've vowed to stop any more atrocities before more of our kind are injured... or worse.\nI have seen a couple hints of corruption in Darkshore already, but I have yet to find any widespread signs. I think it would be logical if the investigation continued with the furbolgs. Would you find one of their camps, and return to me if you see any signs of corruption?","rew":"Experience: 750\n+75 reputation with Darnassus","back":"How goes your search, ‹name›?","done":"This is terrible news indeed, ‹name›.\nWith the furbolgs this close to Auberdine, we will have to prepare ourselves for the inevitable.\nThank you, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"Darkshore","x":39.4,"y":43.5,"n":"Terenthis","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darkshore"]},"6344":{"id":6344,"t":"Nessa Shadowsong","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Nessa Shadowsong.","desc":"A friend of mine, Nessa Shadowsong, is a fishing merchant in Rut'theran Village. She needs a parcel taken to Darkshore, and is looking for someone to help her.\nIf you're interested, then to reach Nessa you must take the portal in Darnassus to Rut'theran Village. You will find the portal west of the Temple Gardens.","rew":"Experience: 210\n+25 reputation with Darnassus","done":"Yes, I have need of a courier who will take a package to Darkshore. Will you help me?\nDarnassus Teldrassil","pins":[{"z":"Darnassus","x":70.7,"y":45.4,"n":"Mydrannul","s":1},{"z":"Teldrassil","x":56.3,"y":92.4,"n":"Nessa Shadowsong","e":1}],"cats":["darnassus"]},"1384":{"id":1384,"t":"Raid on the Kolkar","lv":32,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Maintain your reputation with the Gelkis, and bring 10 Crude Charms to Uthek the Wise in the Gelkis Village in Desolace.\n10 Crude Charm Kolkar Windchaser 30 % , Kolkar Scout 30 % , Kolkar Ambusher 20 % , Kolkar Waylayer 20 % and 4 more\nReach 3000 reputation with Gelkis Clan Centaur","desc":"The Kolkar centaurs think their magic is strong. They do not know magic! They would not know magic if it bit them!\nYou will show them their magic is weak. Go to the Kolkar to the northeast and kill them. Take their charms. Bring me the charms and I will throw them in the fire and laugh!","rew":"Experience: 2,550","back":"You have the charms? You showed the Kolkar they are weak?","done":"You do a good thing for the Gelkis. The Kolkar are weak and will die. Their magic is pathetic and will not save them. You showed them this, and their fear will make them even more feeble!\nAnd in our lands, the feeble soon die.","pins":[{"z":"Desolace","x":36.2,"y":79.2,"n":"Uthek the Wise","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["desolace"]},"93224":{"id":93224,"t":"Carved centaur totems","lv":40,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Acquire 5 Carved Centaur Totems by slaying centaur of any clan throughout Desolace, then return them to Captain Pentigast at Nijel's Point.\n5 Carved Centaur Totem","desc":"It likely comes as no surprise to you that both of the centaur clans are hesitant to accept aid from anyone outside of their clan. This is especially true for folks like you and me - you know, non-centaurs.\nOne thing we all have in common is an understanding that money is power, and we have learned that the local centaur barter with carved wood. If you bring me a few samples of their designs, I can put in a rush order for similar etchings. Perhaps we can buy ourselves an advantage.\nLevel 40 , requires level 30 Difficulty 30 36 38 43 51 Side Alliance Shareable Yes Quest ID 93224","cats":["desolace"]},"6584":{"id":6584,"t":"The Test of Skulls, Chronalis","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Guarding the Caverns of Time in the Tanaris Desert is Chronalis, child of Nozdormu. Destroy him and return his skull to Emberstrife.\nThe Skull of Chronalis Chronalis","desc":"The time watchers, children of Nozdormu - Lord of the Centuriesss...\nIt is three that guard the Caverns of Time, but only one that holds the interests of the Black Flight: The Time Shifter, Chronalis, favored drakeling of Nozdormu.\nSsstrike at this champion, a blow to make even the stoic sands of time weep. Return to me with his skull.","rew":"Experience: 6,600","back":"Ironically, whelp, time is of the essencccce.","done":"The most hated remainsss...\nDustwallow Marsh Tanaris","pins":[{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":56.7,"y":87.7,"n":"Emberstrife","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["dustwallow-marsh"]},"5544":{"id":5544,"t":"Carrion Grubbage","lv":56,"min":52,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Seek out the Carrion Grubs and Devourers of the region. Slay them and harvest their meat. Return to Tirion Fordring when you have gathered 15 Slabs of Carrion Worm Meat.\n15 Slab of Carrion Worm Meat Carrion Grub 80 % , Carrion Devourer 80 %","desc":"My food supplies are running low, ‹race›. I am ashamed to admit that I might not have enough food to share with you.\nCould you assist an old man with a simple task? Around here, the only manner of beast unaffected by the ravages of the Plague are the Carrion worms. While rather bland in taste, the meat of the worms can easily be preserved to last for months. I will need several hundred pounds to restock for the coming winter!","rew":"Experience: 5,800","back":"You will grow to tolerate the taste, ‹race›.","done":"May the Light watch over you! Bless you, young one.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":5.2,"y":35.6,"n":"Tirion Fordring","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"9224":{"id":9224,"t":"Epic Armaments of Battle - Honored Amongst the Dawn","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"For 75 Insignias of the Dawn and 75 Insignias of the Crusade you may choose an item from the Argent Dawn's treasure cache.\n75 Insignia of the Dawn\n75 Insignia of the Crusade","desc":"Greetings, friend. Have you insignias of the Dawn or the Crusade that you would like to redeem for items of great power?\nI must warn you; purchases made at honored reputation with the Dawn come with an extremely hefty surcharge. I would advise that you gain a better reputation with the Dawn before moving forward with your plans.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nAmulet of the Dawn Bracers of Hope Bracers of Subterfuge Medallion of the Dawn Talisman of Ascendance The Purifier\n+100 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"Choose carefully. There are no refunds.","done":"Good day, ‹name›. It was a pleasure doing business with you.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.8,"y":50.2,"n":"Quartermaster Miranda Breechlock","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"6024":{"id":6024,"t":"Hameya's Plea","lv":60,"min":54,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill Infiltrator Hameya. Use his key on the Mound of Dirt behind the Undercroft.\nHameya's Key Infiltrator Hameya","desc":"Kill me. Before it's too late.\nI am Hameya. While traveling to Zul'Mashar, my brethren and I ate some bad meat... and we changed. We are infected.\nI can feel the lich's words now, urging me to reach Zul'Mashar and infect more of my people. I cannot resist, and so I wrote this scroll before my will left me.\nI buried a chest in dirt next to a wagon behind this crypt, but only my key will open it. I have the key. If you want my treasure, then find me.\nKill me. Before it's too late.","rew":"You will receive:\nHameya's Slayer Hameya's Cloak\nMoney: 90 0 gold, 90 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,600","back":"This chest buried here is securely locked.","done":"Hameya's chest is opened!!","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":22.9,"y":73,"n":"Torn Scroll","s":1},{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":23.6,"y":73.8,"n":"Mound of Dirt","e":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"5464":{"id":5464,"t":"Menethil's Gift","lv":60,"min":57,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 8,300 experience instead of 8,800, 0.94 times as much.","obj":"Take the Soulbound Keepsake to Leonid Barthalomew in Eastern Plaguelands.\nSoulbound Keepsake\nProvided: Soulbound Keepsake","desc":"The soul of the fallen clings to that which represents its former life and transforms the item into a soulbound keepsake. You pick the item up and place it in your pack.","rew":"Experience: 8,300\n+150 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"<Leonid shudders.>","done":"As the soul clung to the keepsake, so shall it cling to the physical form of Ras Frostwhisper.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.9,"y":48.3,"n":"Leonid Barthalomew the Revered","e":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"98824":{"id":98824,"t":"Prehistoric prism","lv":31,"min":24,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring the Titan Relic to High Explorer Magellas in Ironforge's Hall of Explorers.\nTitan Relic","desc":"With titan-like inscriptions like that on its facets, nothing less than Ironforge's Hall of Explorers is the right place to bring it.\nI'd like to think that you'll be noted in the history for it in the catalogue -- \"Recovered by ‹name›! Authenticated by Prospector Whelgar...\" Ah, I'm gettin' meself carried away.\nHigh Explorer Magellas will receive you, and given the exquisite nature of what you carry, will surely be most generously appreciative should you donate it to the museum.\nGood find!","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nExplorer's League Dustcover Healer's Staff Heavehammer\nMoney: 60 0 gold, 60 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,150\nWetlands Ironforge","pins":[{"z":"Wetlands","x":38.8,"y":52.2,"n":"Prospector Whelgar","s":1},{"z":"Ironforge","x":69.6,"y":18.6,"n":"High Explorer Magellas","e":1}],"cats":["excavation-site-wetlands-dungeon"]},"4104":{"id":4104,"t":"Salve via Mining","lv":55,"min":48,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"4 Tainted Vitriol Gold Vein 50 % , Ooze Covered Gold Vein 50 % , Gold Vein 50 % , Mithril Deposit 50 % and 4 more","rew":"You will receive:\n2 Cenarion Plant Salve\nExperience: 4,200","back":"If you possess a Cenarion beacon while mining in Felwood, you will be able to see tainted vitriol that corrupts a vein of raw metal. I know how to purify that vitriol and turn it into a reagent that goes into making Cenarion plant salve. You will then use that salve on plants you find in the wild that need saving.\nIf you have collected any tainted vitriol, I'll give you some Cenarion plant salve I have already prepared.","done":"Very well then, here's some Cenarion plant salve. If you find more vitriol when you mine in Felwood, remember to hold on to it for me! The more of it you find, the more salve I will be able to make.","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":54.1,"y":86.8,"n":"Arathandris Silversky","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"2904":{"id":2904,"t":"A Fine Mess","lv":30,"min":20,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 20 instead of 24. Gives 5,800 experience instead of 2,450, 2.37 times as much. New rewards: Technician's Bracers. Partly read from what the game server sent. Its experience counts the level 30 build, which","obj":"Escort Kernobee to the Clockwerk Run exit and then report to Scooty in Booty Bay.","desc":"<Kernobee groans.> Wha.. What happened?\nThe last thing I remember is being captured by a group of dark iron dwarves, beaten to within an inch of my life and then thrown in here with these filthy troggs.\nGet me out of here, ‹name›!\nHere's the plan: Lead me to the exit; if we make it out alive, you go to Booty Bay and let Scooty know that I went to Ratchet to warn Tinkerwiz of the dark iron's involvement in the making of that super rig.\nLet's get going!","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nFire-welded Bracers Fairywing Mantle Technician's Bracers\nNew in Forever: Technician's Bracers.\nExperience: 5,800","back":"Eh? Kernobee is alive??","done":"I suppose you should be rewarded for bringing Kernobee back to us in one piece, ‹name›. If you go back to Gnomeregan, these might give you the edge you'll need in defeating that good-for-nothing backstabber, Mekgineer Thermaplugg.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":27.6,"y":77.5,"n":"Scooty","e":1}],"cats":["gnomeregan"]},"9304":{"id":9304,"t":"Document from the Front","lv":60,"min":45,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 45 instead of 55.","obj":"Take the Smudged Document to the Keeper of the Rolls at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands.\nA Smudged Document\nProvided: A Smudged Document","desc":"You found this letter on one of the many Scourge minions you've slain. From its appearance and smell, it has been with the undead for some time. Perhaps someone at Light's Hope Chapel would be interested in examining it further...","back":"Yes? What do you have there?","done":"How tragic. These words, clearly meant for someone the soldier loved, never made it to their destination. The events detailed happened years ago; I'm not sure if the intended recipient still lives.\nThere is hope yet, however. With the names and information he gives, I might be able to locate the family! It will take some research, but the librarian in Stormwind owes me a favor...\nThank you for bringing this to me. With your help, we may be able to grant someone peace of mind at least.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.2,"y":50.6,"n":"Keeper of the Rolls","e":1}],"cats":["invasion"]},"5144":{"id":5144,"t":"Elemental Leatherworking","lv":55,"min":40,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 2 Heart of Fire, 2 Globe of Water, 2 Core of Earth, and 2 Breath of Wind to Sarah Tanner in Searing Gorge.\nCompleting this quest will give you access to the Elemental Leatherworking arts.\nThe completion of this quest will prevent you from learning Dragonscale Leatherworking and Tribal Leatherworking; be sure this is the path you wish to follow before doing so.\n2 Heart of Fire Baron Charr 69.9 % , Prince Skaldrenox 41.7 % , Golemagg the Incinerator 30 % , Baron Geddon 30 % and 4 more\n2 Globe of Water Princess Tempestria 77.1 % , Lord Skwol 47.6 % , Hydrospawn 20 % , Muck Splash 16.1 % and 4 more\n2 Core of Earth Avalanchion 78.6 % , Baron Kazum 57.4 % , Golemagg the Incinerator 30 % , Garr 30 % and 4 more\n2 Breath of Wind Gusting Vortex 83.8 % , The Windreaver 76 % , Living Storm 66.7 % , High Marshal Whirlaxis 35.9 % and 4 more","desc":"Elemental leatherworking is what I know, and if you're willing to open your mind to the greater powers of substance, I will share with you all there is to learn.\nKnow this, ‹class›: by choosing this path you agree never to learn dragonscale or tribal leatherworking; there is only room for practice of one of the three arts. Furthermore, I'll need adequate proof that you are in tune with the elements of nature; to that end, bring me the purest essences of fire, water, earth, and wind.","rew":"You will learn: Elemental Leatherworking\nExperience: 4,200\n+200 reputation with Leatherworking - Elemental","back":"Making this kind of leather-based armor requires patience and dedication. Once you have cast your lot with the elements, there is no turning your back on them. Bring me proof of your worthiness, and we'll get started.","done":"You've cast your lot, and the elements accept you. Once I have finished my tutelage, you shall command the will to craft the finest of leather garbs.\nTo train in the art for the future, simply speak to me and I will make available any knowledge that you have yet to commit as yours.","pins":[{"z":"Searing Gorge","x":63.6,"y":76,"n":"Sarah Tanner","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["leatherworking"]},"1944":{"id":1944,"t":"Waters of Xavian","lv":26,"min":26,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Xavian Water Sample to Deino in Orgrimmar.\nXavian Water Sample\nProvided: Deino's Flask","desc":"The fabled city of Xavian lies nestled deep within eastern Ashenvale, and tales of its ancient knowledge are well known among the learned. It is said that the waters of Xavian hold vast magical powers.\nI would have a sample of those waters, from their source.\nTake this flask and go to Xavian. Gather water from the bottom of its highest waterfall, and return to me. And use care as you move through that ancient city--satyrs now hold the ruins and do not like mages prying into their affairs.","rew":"Experience: 2,100","back":"I am pleased you have returned with your skin intact, ‹name›. Do you have the water sample? I am eager to study its properties.","done":"Ah, very good. I trust the satyrs of Xavian gave you little trouble?\nThank you, ‹name›. I will study this sample of Xavian water immediately.","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":38.4,"y":86.1,"n":"Deino","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["mage"]},"7064":{"id":7064,"t":"Corruption of Earth and Seed","lv":51,"min":45,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Slay Princess Theradras and return to Selendra near Shadowprey Village in Desolace.\nPrincess Theradras slain","desc":"Deep in Maraudon lives an evil creature of chaos--Princess Theradras is an elemental force of earth related to the Old Gods. Ages ago, she and Zaetar, first son of Cenarius, began a relationship. The offspring of their time together became known to the people of Kalimdor as centaur. Ever-thankful creatures, the centaur killed Zaetar, and now hold Zaetar's remains. My quest here is to find those powerful enough to slay Theradras so we may recover Zaetar's remains before returning to Stonetalon.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nThrash Blade Resurgence Rod Verdant Keeper's Aim\nExperience: 6,100\n+150 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"I would prefer to fight this battle on our own, but we are left with no other options--we need those more powerful, and the races of Azeroth have proven without a doubt they can overcome such things when they work together. So it is to you we turn for help.\nI only hope it is enough.\nZaetar, brother to Remulos, brought many pains to this world, and ultimately it caused his own death. I just hope I have not caused more death by asking you to aid us.","done":"This is most wonderful news, ‹name›! Thank you!\nI will speak with Marandis and ask his wisdom on the topic of Zaetar's remains, but at least you have overcome the hardest of the tasks.\nI was told that if we were successful in our mission, I had permission to reward those who aided us. I was given these items as tokens from our people--you may choose one.\nDesolace Stonetalon Mountains","pins":[{"z":"Desolace","x":26.9,"y":77.7,"n":"Selendra","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["maraudon"]},"98424":{"id":98424,"t":"Fizsprockets notes","lv":10,"min":5,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Collect the rest of Supervisor Fizsprocket's pages inside The Venture Co. Mine and bring them to Morin Cloudstalker near Bloodhoof Village.\nShredder Operation Instructions\nBarrens Operations Best Practices\nOne \"Gerenzo\", of Stonetalon\nMulgore Expansion Plans","desc":"Some particularly worn papers are held separately, folded in Fizsprocket's inside breast pocket.\nThey seem to detail important information that could be used against the Venture Co. and its operations in the region. It would be prudent to look for more before returning to Morin Cloudstalker.","back":"What is it you bring me, ‹class›?","done":"Ah, this is most valuable knowledge. I thank you for your efforts.\n<Morin looks through the notes.>\nIt seems our next move is clear.","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":53,"y":60.2,"n":"Morin Cloudstalker","e":1}],"cats":["mulgore"]},"7784":{"id":7784,"t":"The Lord of Blackrock","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with High Overlord Saurfang in Orgrimmar. He stands waiting for you in the Valley of Strength.","desc":"Seek out High Overlord Saurfang in the Valley of Strength.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nMaster Dragonslayer's Medallion Master Dragonslayer's Orb Master Dragonslayer's Ring\nExperience: 9,950\n+200 reputation with Orgrimmar\n+200 reputation with Darkspear Trolls\n+200 reputation with Thunder Bluff\n+200 reputation with Undercity","done":"Choose your reward so that I may mount the head of the beast for all to see.\nOrgrimmar Silithus","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":31.7,"y":37.8,"n":"Thrall","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":51,"y":75.7,"n":"High Overlord Saurfang","e":1},{"z":"Silithus","x":45.2,"y":44.1,"n":"High Overlord Saurfang","e":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"1784":{"id":1784,"t":"The Tome of Divinity","lv":13,"min":12,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Retrieve a Dark Iron Script from the Dark Iron dwarves near Helm's Bed, and return to Muiredon Battleforge in Ironforge.\nDark Iron Script Dark Iron Spy 50 %","desc":"Before I fell in battle, Muiredon and I had almost defeated one of the Dark Iron spies near that small house. We witnessed their captain passing orders to them, and sought to kill him and take the orders.\nSome of the council in Ironforge do not yet believe the presence of Dark Iron dwarves exists in Dun Morogh. By attaining one of those scripts, we'll not only have proof of their movements, but possibly an idea of what they're planning.\nGet one of those scripts and take it back to Muiredon, ‹name›.","rew":"Experience: 675","back":"Yer back! I'm glad to see it, ‹name›. My wounds are healed and I'm about ready to return to Helm's Bed lake as soon as I c'n convince me wife that I'll be fine.","done":"Haha! You've done it! Ya saved Narm, and ya found the proof me wife needs to take to the council. Yer a blessin' o' the Light if I ever saw one... not includin' me wife o' course.\nThank ya again, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":78.3,"y":58.1,"n":"Narm Faulk","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":54.9,"y":22.4,"n":"Muiredon Battleforge","e":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"5624":{"id":5624,"t":"Garments of the Light","lv":4,"min":5,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Guard Roberts and heal his wounds using Lesser Heal (Rank 2). Afterwards, grant him Power Word: Fortitude and then return to Priestess Josetta in Goldshire.\nHeal and fortify Guard Roberts","desc":"Normally I put forth a small challenge to followers of the Light to test their skill. I want to see if they are worthy of wearing their first robes--a sign that the church outwardly approves of the priest/priestess and supports him/her.\nBut this situation is a bit different. One of Goldshire's citizens saw an injured guard near the lake to the east of here. His name is Roberts. Find him, heal him, fortify his body and return here. If you can do that for me, then I will consider your test complete.","rew":"You will receive:\nFriar's Robes of the Light\nExperience: 270","back":"As you may have already learned, our healing magics are vital to the survival of our people in these harsh times--especially to adventurers and heroes who take up arms and magic to fight back so many different threats.\nYou would do well to always remember how important that skill is. That, coupled with Fortitude, make your companions far more capable in battle since they will be able to stand up to a greater number of blows.\nDo not let anyone dismiss how powerful your magics are.","done":"Excellent, ‹name›. With one more healthy guard out there to help the town, we'll be that much safer. I'm glad to see you're already learning to use your abilities wisely. If you feel you are ready for more training at any time, please come back to me. But for now, take this robe. It will let others know that you are one of our order. If you don't want to wear it, that's fine. Later there will be more tests and this robe isn't necessary for those.","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":43.3,"y":65.7,"n":"Priestess Josetta","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["priest"]},"94824":{"id":94824,"t":"Confounding flash","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak to High Priestess Mims in Ironforge.","desc":"Time's come for you to head to Stormwind, ‹name›. High Priestess Mims in the Hall of Mysteries commands you to come speak with her. Gotta be somethin' really good or really bad for the High Priestess to want you there personally, but I'm guessin' you've only done well for yourself and it's a good thing that she wants to speak to ya.\nBut don't waste too much time 'round here. I'd head there as soon as you can.","done":"You took your time arriving, Papi. But you can be excused given your dedicated service to the Light. Please pay close attention to this lesson.\nDun Morogh Ironforge","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":47.2,"y":52.2,"n":"Maxan Anvol","s":1},{"z":"Ironforge","x":24.8,"y":10,"n":"High Priestess Mims","e":1}],"cats":["priest"]},"1144":{"id":1144,"t":"Willix the Importer","lv":30,"min":22,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 22 instead of 23. Gives 7,250 experience instead of 3,050, 2.38 times as much. New rewards: Boar Signet. Partly read from what the game server sent.","obj":"Escort Willix the Importer out of Razorfen Kraul.","desc":"At last, help has arrived!\nYou have no clue how long I've been held prisoner here. I can't remember the last time I saw the outside of this place.\nYou see, I am an entrepreneur. Always out for a copper, as they say. I caught wind that Mebok Mizzyrix was paying well for Blueleaf Tuber from this here pig pen. I figured it would be an easy in, easy out kind of affair. As you can see, I was a bit wrong!\nAnyway, if you'd be so kind as to help me get out of here, I'll make it worth your while.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nMonkey Ring Snake Hoop Tiger Band Boar Signet\nNew in Forever: Boar Signet.\nExperience: 7,250\n+150 reputation with Ratchet","done":"Thanks again, friend! I told you I'd make it worth your while.\nStart Willix the Importer Razorfen Kraul End Willix the Importer Razorfen Kraul Level 30 , requires level 22 Difficulty 22 26 28 33 38 Side Human, Orc, Dwarf, Night Elf, Undead, Tauren, Gnome, Troll Type Dungeon Shareable No Quest ID 1144","cats":["razorfen-kraul"]},"8824":{"id":8824,"t":"Ten Commendation Signets","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"10 Horde Commendation Signet","back":"I accept commendation signets from adventurers who have received them in the line of duty. For each set of ten that you hand to me, I'll make sure that you receive a significant acknowledgement of your deeds with Undercity. I also accept single tokens, but at a much reduced rate of recognition. We are much more interested in greater feats of duty, though no feat will be ignored.\nWith that said, I'll gladly take your signets if you are ready to hand in a set.","done":"Excellent! It is no small sacrifice that you've made to earn these signets, and you will be acknowledged for your service appropriately. It's adventurers like you, ‹name›, that truly make a difference.\nLet me know if you have additional signets to hand in; I'll gladly help you out with whatever ones you need exchanged.\nOrgrimmar Undercity","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":30,"y":70.1,"n":"Darkspear Commendation Officer","s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":61.9,"y":45.3,"n":"Officer Gothena","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["reputation"]},"5384":{"id":5384,"t":"Kirtonos the Herald","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return to the Scholomance with the Blood of Innocents. Find the porch and place the Blood of Innocents in the brazier. Kirtonos will come to feast upon your soul.\nFight valiantly, do not give an inch! Destroy Kirtonos and return to Eva Sarkhoff.\nKirtonos the Herald slain\nProvided: Blood of Innocents","desc":"This is it, ‹name›.\n<Eva points to the vial inside the bag.>\nThe blood of innocents. The purest blood, used to appease Krastinov's master.\nIt is with this blood that Kirtonos may be summoned. It is with this blood, then, that Kirtonos must be destroyed.\nTake the blood to the porch. Place it upon the brazier. Kirtonos will come - he cannot resist. When he appears, unleash the fury and wrath of a thousand innocent deaths upon him.\nShould you succeed, you will earn more than just our gratitude.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nPenelope's Rose Mirah's Song\nYou will also receive:\nSpectral Essence\nExperience: 8,300","back":"Be wary, Kirtonos is a seasoned fighter.","done":"With the death of Kirtonos, a chapter in the horrible tale of Scholomance comes to a close. There is, however, more to be done. Others here are now aware of your brave acts. Take this, ‹name›. It is a piece of our own essence. It will allow you to communicate with the other lost souls of Caer Darrow.","pins":[{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":70.2,"y":73.7,"n":"Eva Sarkhoff","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["scholomance"]},"7704":{"id":7704,"t":"Look at the Size of It!","lv":50,"min":45,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take Chambermaid Pillaclencher's Pillow to Evonice Sootsmoker in the Searing Gorge.\nChambermaid Pillaclencher's Pillow Pillaclencher's Ornate Pillow\nProvided: Chambermaid Pillaclencher's Pillow","desc":"Well, well, well... Isn't this a surprise. The Chambermaid had a gigantic ornate pillow and now it's yours. Evonice Sootsmoker will definitely want to get her grubby little hands all over this item. Take it to her and see if she'll offer you any goodies for your trouble.","rew":"You will receive:\nEvonice's Landin' Pilla\nExperience: 4,700\n+100 reputation with Thorium Brotherhood","done":"This is better than even I could have thought possible! The Chambermaid's magical pillow is mine! You better believe you're going to get a nice reward for this accomplishment, ‹name›!","pins":[{"z":"Searing Gorge","x":38.4,"y":27.7,"n":"Evonice Sootsmoker","e":1}],"cats":["searing-gorge"]},"8744":{"id":8744,"t":"A Carefully Wrapped Present","lv":1,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nCarefully Wrapped Present","done":"The tag on this present reads:\nTo ‹name›,\nMay your feast of Great-Winter be merry and bright!\nDun Morogh Orgrimmar","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":56.5,"y":31.6,"n":"Carefully Wrapped Present","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":52.4,"y":69.5,"n":"Carefully Wrapped Present","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["seasonal"]},"6984":{"id":6984,"t":"A Smokywood Pastures Thank You!","lv":60,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Renamed from A Smokywood Pastures Thank You!.","obj":"Speak with Great-father Winter in Orgrimmar.","desc":"We at Smokywood Pastures appreciate the recovery of the stolen treats, ‹name›. For that, we'd like to offer you a special gift... presented by none other than Great-father Winter himself!\nPlease, speak with Great-father Winter, and he will give you your Feast of Winter Veil gift from us here at Smokywood Pastures. From our farm to your plate, it's always Smokywood Pastures wholesome goodness... thanks to you, of course!","rew":"You will receive:\nSmokywood Pastures Special Gift\nExperience: 4,950\n+100 reputation with Steamwheedle Cartel","done":"Ho ho hello, adventurer!\nThe goblins told me that you have earned a special gift this holiday season, and I am pleased to give it to you. Here you go - have a wondrous Feast of Winter Veil this and every season in the future.","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":53.3,"y":66.5,"n":"Kaymard Copperpinch","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":52.5,"y":69.2,"n":"Great-father Winter","e":1}],"cats":["seasonal"]},"8904":{"id":8904,"t":"Dangerous Love","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Get a Guardian's Moldy Card and bring it to Fenstad Argyle in the Undercity.\nGuardian's Moldy Card","desc":"There's something unnatural about this epidemic of love. It's disgusting, and as it lowers our defenses, it could be a threat to the all of us.\nIt's bad enough that so many of our people are caught up in this ridiculous behavior. But I think that it has spread even to our guardians, who should be immune to such things.\nFind one of our guardians and see if they've been caught up in this foolishness.","back":"Was I right to worry? Have our idiot guardians been overcome?","done":"So it is true. This is unbelievable. How could this have happened? Let me think for a moment. There must be a reason behind this.","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":66.7,"y":44.7,"n":"Fenstad Argyle","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["seasonal"]},"8984":{"id":8984,"t":"The Source Revealed","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Apothecary Staffron Lerent in the Hillsbrad Foothills past Ravenholdt Manor.","desc":"Look, the actions of a rogue apothecary are not my concern. If he's undermining our efforts, then let me be the first to point you in the right direction\nIf he's innocent, then he's got nothing to hide, right?\nI purchased the goods from Apothecary Staffron Lerent. He's working in a secluded area past Ravenholdt Manor in the hills over Hillsbrad. To be honest with you, I thought he was a little odd.","done":"Yes, I made those fragrances. Wonderful smell, isn't it? Irresistible.\nOnce the warriors of Alliance and Horde alike are smitten with these feelings of love, they will be powerless to stop the rise of the Shadow Council.\nThey will be weakened, unprepared. As they worry for their loved ones, they will lose their edge.\nThe solution was so simple. Why did it take me so long to come upon it? The weakness of all is through the heart. And there is nothing you can do to stop the inevitable.\nUndercity Alterac Mountains","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":71.3,"y":28.3,"n":"Mara Rennick","s":1},{"z":"Alterac Mountains","x":89.5,"y":75.5,"n":"Apothecary Staffron Lerent","e":1}],"cats":["seasonal"]},"2984":{"id":2984,"t":"Call of Fire","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Kranal Fiss in the Barrens.","desc":"Long has it been since you were last tested, ‹name›. You have shown patience thus far in your studies, but the time has come for you to learn more. The time has come for you to learn about destruction... and chaos. The element of fire is yours for the understanding, if you're prepared to pay for it.\nSeek out Kranal Fiss in the Barrens. He lives in a small dwelling north of the Crossroads, but be mindful, if you've reached the night elf lands, you've gone too far.","rew":"Experience: 420","done":"Hmmm, Narm sent you to me, did he?\nbWell then, Narm could always be trusted, so that must mean you're ready to take part of the next sapta--the sapta of fire.\nI see it in your eyes already, the burning, the desire. You've tasted power, and now you're ready for more of it. Patience, ‹name›. Remember what earth taught you. Power and destruction will come easily, but you must still know when to stay your hand.\nMulgore The Barrens","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":47.4,"y":62.5,"n":"Narm Skychaser","s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":56,"y":19.9,"n":"Kranal Fiss","e":1}],"cats":["shaman"]},"1464":{"id":1464,"t":"Fire Sapta","lv":13,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Telf Joolam for another Fire Sapta.","rew":"You will receive:\nFire Sapta","done":"May fire burn within your heart, ‹name›.\nThe elements await you.","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":38.6,"y":59,"n":"Telf Joolam","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["shaman"]},"96264":{"id":96264,"t":"Elemental aid","lv":33,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Defeat Charlga Razorflank in Razorfen Kraul and collect information on the quilboar's plans.\nTattered Note","desc":"So yer a big shot shaman now, eh? Ye've mastered the elements and want tae put 'em to good use? I think I got just the thing.\nIf ye want the elements' respect, ye gotta repay yer debts to 'em. They help you, you help them. And right now they need all the help they can get from those who would abuse their power.\nEarth's rumblin', ‹name›. It speaks of the quilboar amassin' for some ritual of terrible power. We need tae go investigate their kraul and see what they're up to. Bring me back whatever ye find.","pins":[{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":59.8,"y":27.6,"n":"Veyric Thunderhame","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["shaman"]},"424":{"id":424,"t":"Arugal's Folly","lv":15,"min":12,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill Grimson the Pale and bring his head to Dalar Dawnweaver at the Sepulcher.\nHead of Grimson Grimson the Pale","desc":"It will indeed take me longer than I had thought to uncover the dark secrets behind the enchantments Arugal was using.\nBut in the meantime I need you to take care of a slight problem our Darkstalkers have discovered. It seems that Arugal let his magic spread to the Deep Elem Mine in the hills to the southeast.\nThe mine would prove to be quite a resource for Varimathras's advance.\nI want you to behead the tainted foreman of the mine, Grimson the Pale. With his death, the mine shall be ours.","rew":"Money: 7 0 gold, 7 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,050\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"Has Grimson the Pale been slain? Varimathras will not be pleased if we ignore his bidding.","done":"Most excellent. The mine will provide superb resources for our forces as we spread throughout Silverpine and into Azeroth.","pins":[{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":44.2,"y":39.8,"n":"Dalar Dawnweaver","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["silverpine-forest"]},"344":{"id":344,"t":"Brother Paxton","lv":24,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Brother Paxton in the Northshire Abbey.","desc":"The Stresses of Iron? Yes, I know the book. Quite a good one, written by the Dwarven miner Margulf Blaggon a few decades ago. He spent most his time deep in the mountains of Khaz Modan, digging ore. Smart fellow!\nBut where was I? Oh yes, the Stresses of Iron! I'm afraid the book was moved to the Northshire Abbey. The caretaker of the Abbey's library, Brother Paxton, wanted to make a copy of the book for his own shelves.\nBut that was months ago. I wonder why it's taking him so long...","rew":"Experience: 490\n+25 reputation with Stormwind","done":"Mr. Sheaf is wondering where his book is? Well this is a tad embarrassing. I have the book, but I'm still making my copy and I'm not quite ready to give the original up!\nStormwind City Elwynn Forest","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":77.1,"y":30.2,"n":"Milton Sheaf","s":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":49.6,"y":40.4,"n":"Brother Paxton","e":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"95384":{"id":95384,"t":"Partial mystical notes","lv":40,"min":32,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring the partial scroll to Dudd Fizzlescroll in Booty Bay.\nPartial Mystical Notes","rew":"You will receive:\nDudd's Second-Favorite Wand\nMoney: 50 0 gold, 50 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,150\n+50 reputation with Booty Bay\nStart an item: Item 213127 Level 40 , requires level 32 Difficulty 32 36 38 43 51 Side Both factions Quest ID 95384","cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"584":{"id":584,"t":"Bloodscalp Clan Heads","lv":41,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Gan'zulah's Head and Nezzliok's Head to the bubbling cauldron at the Grom'gol Base Camp.\nGan'zulah's Head Gan'zulah\nNezzliok's Head Nezzliok the Dire","desc":"Yenniku was not among the heads, and I thank the Great Serpent for it. But we are no closer to finding him.\nWe must know the truth, and I fear that only the Bloodscalp chief and his witchdoctor know it. They are the enemies of the Darkspear tribe and will not speak freely, so we must force the truth from their dead lips!\nBring me the heads of Gan'zulah and Nezzliok the Dire and place them within this cauldron.\nThey are deep within Zul'Kunda. Bring their heads...we will then make them talk.","rew":"Experience: 3,300\n+100 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"The greenish broth within the cauldron bubbles.","done":"You place the heads of Gan'zulah and Nezzliok within the cauldron...","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":32.2,"y":27.7,"n":"Nimboya","s":1},{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":32.2,"y":27.6,"n":"Bubbling Cauldron","e":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"93464":{"id":93464,"t":"The visiting mage","lv":38,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Find the mage in Desolace who knows about the power of draenethyst.","desc":"Allow me to admit something, ‹name›. While draenethyst is sacred to us, and keeps us sane, none here fully understand it.\nI recall a mage who once came to the Harborage, from Desolace. A human by the name of Azore. He feared the power of the draenethyst; said it shouldn't fall into the wrong hands.\nAt the time, we drove him away to protect what was ours. Lately, however, I find myself wondering what exactly he knew.\nI ask that you find this mage, ‹race›. His knowledge could be of immense value to us.","rew":"Money: 11 0 gold, 11 silver, 0 copper Experience: 700\nLevel 38 , requires level 30 Difficulty 30 34 36 41 48 Side Both factions Shareable Yes Quest ID 93464\nThe chain\n2 quests from level 38 to 40, 3,850 XP in all.\n1 [ 38 ] The Visiting Mage this quest\nFind the mage in Desolace who knows about the power of draenethyst.\n700 XP\n2 [ 40 ] Notes on Draenethyst\nTake Gimashi's notes on Draenethyst, and bring them back to Azore Aldamort.\n3,150 XP","cats":["swamp-of-sorrows"]},"4504":{"id":4504,"t":"Super Sticky","lv":54,"min":48,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Collect 12 samples of Super Sticky Tar for Tran'rek in Gadgetzan.\n12 Super Sticky Tar Tar Creeper 33 % , Tar Lord 33 % , Tar Beast 33 % , Tar Lurker 33 %","desc":"I'm always looking for a quick way to earn a gold, ‹name›. If you help me with my newest idea, I'll let you in on a little of the profit. How does that sound to you?\nI thought so!\nHead to the tar pits in northern Un'Goro Crater, and collect me some tar. Not just any tar, now, you'll need to get it from the beasts that live around the tar pits. Regular tar just simply isn't sticky enough.\nThe plant-like creatures contain chlorophyll in their skin, and mixed with the tar, it's super sticky!","rew":"Money: 1 65 1 gold, 65 silver, 0 copper Experience: 5,450\n+100 reputation with Gadgetzan","back":"Tran'rek's done it again -- this super sticky glue will be all the rage!","done":"Yes, this tar is just the stuff...\nHey, wait a minute, my hands... I can't seem to get them apart...\nMaybe this wasn't such a good idea. Oh, but wait! Super sticky tar remover! That's where the real money is!\nTanaris Un'Goro Crater","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":51.6,"y":26.8,"n":"Tran'rek","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"8584":{"id":8584,"t":"Never Ask Me About My Business","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Narain Soothfancy in Tanaris wants you to speak with Dirge Quikcleave in Gadgetzan.","desc":"If there is one thing that you should know about me, it is this: NEVER ask me about my business! I work with things you simply cannot understand. Like for example: Do you know what a psychotronic muzzledorf is? Of course you don't! And that's why we leave the planning to me and the fetching to you.\nAs I said earlier, if this is going to work, we're going to need a 500 pound chicken.\nHead to Gadgetzan and speak with Dirge Quikcleave - he'll get you started on finding a suitable specimen.","rew":"Experience: 650","done":"<Dirge scratches his head.>\nA 500 pound chicken? There's no such thing! Not anymore, at least. I knew of such a chicken... The Black Chicken of Death...\n<Dirge's voice trails off.>\nBut yes, nobody ever saw that chicken and lived to tell the tale. I've got an idea that could benefit the both of us, kid.","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":65.2,"y":18.6,"n":"Narain Soothfancy","s":1},{"z":"Tanaris","x":52.6,"y":28.1,"n":"Dirge Quikcleave","e":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"98024":{"id":98024,"t":"Journey to the crossroads","lv":13,"min":7,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Report To Thork at The Crossroads in The Barrens.","desc":"After journeying here from the elemental plane, the problems our lands face may seem small. Rest assured, the dangers the horde faces are very real, and you will grow formidable should you survive your service.\nIf you'd like to get started doing some good in our world, travel southwest to the vast lands known as the Barrens. There is a settlement there known as the Crossroads. The proud citizens there are ever in need of aid.\nGo with honor, adventurer!","rew":"Money: 3 0 gold, 3 silver, 0 copper Experience: 460\n+25 reputation with Windshapers","done":"What's this? An elf? And you say the Warchief sent you?\n<Thork grunts sharply as he looks you up and down.>\nYou look a little skinny to me, but it matters not. Out here you'll either thrive and survive, or you'll die. That is the way of things in these lands.\nOrgrimmar The Barrens","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":32,"y":37.8,"n":"Thrall","s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":51.4,"y":30.8,"n":"Thork","e":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"5064":{"id":5064,"t":"Grimtotem Spying","lv":28,"min":24,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Locate and retrieve the three Secret Notes in Darkcloud Pinnacle.\nSecret Note #1 Pitted Iron Chest , Document Chest\nSecret Note #2 Pitted Iron Chest , Document Chest , Document Chest\nSecret Note #3 Pitted Iron Chest , Document Chest , Document Chest","desc":"‹name›, you have served us well in the past, so I now entrust to you an important mission. The Grimtotem Clan is up to something secretive. Three agents of unknown origin were seen visiting the Grimtotem over the recent weeks. We discovered that separate chests in Darkcloud Pinnacle hold these guarded messages.\n‹name›, if you succeed in this dangerous mission, I will reward you in kind.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nDesert Shoulders Tundra Boots Grimtoll Wristguards\nExperience: 2,300\n+100 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"Have you discovered what the Grimtotem are up to?","done":"Great Spirit Totem! This is dire news indeed. I must begin to plan for whatever may come.\n‹name›, as promised, here is your reward for your brave service.","pins":[{"z":"Thousand Needles","x":45.7,"y":50.7,"n":"Cliffwatcher Longhorn","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["thousand-needles"]},"4904":{"id":4904,"t":"Free at Last","lv":29,"min":25,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Escort Lakota Windsong from the Darkcloud Pinnacle, and then talk to Thalia Amberhide at Freewind Post.","desc":"Arnak thinks we're going to be married... but after I declined his offer he came back that night and kidnapped me. My brother tried to stop him, but Arnak was too strong. He... he slew my brother and then brought me here. My poor brother...\n‹name›, could you escort me out of the Darkcloud Pinnacle? Please... I need to get back to Thalia! She must be worried sick about me.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nWindsong Cinch Windsong Drape\nExperience: 2,350\n+100 reputation with Thunder Bluff","done":"Thank you, ‹name›. Deep in my bones I knew that she would find her way back to me. She told me of your bravery and how you helped her escape. These items belonged to her brother. I know she would want you to have them.","pins":[{"z":"Thousand Needles","x":37.9,"y":26.4,"n":"Lakota Windsong","s":1},{"z":"Thousand Needles","x":46,"y":51.6,"n":"Thalia Amberhide","e":1}],"cats":["thousand-needles"]},"744":{"id":744,"t":"Preparation for Ceremony","lv":11,"min":7,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Collect 6 Azure Feathers and 6 Bronze Feathers, and bring them to Eyahn Eagletalon in Thunder Bluff.\n6 Azure Feather Windfury Sorceress 80 %\n6 Bronze Feather Windfury Matriarch 80 %","desc":"‹name›, my brother soon stands before Chief Bloodhoof, and it is my honor to make his headdress for him.\nI want to ask a favor of you while I finish tanning these leather straps. There is not time for me to find enough feathers, and I was wondering, would you gather more for me?\nYou can find feathers of the correct size from the harpies residing far to the north and northwest of Thunder Bluff. I need only 6 azure and 6 bronze feathers to complete the design.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nBound Harness Tribal Warrior's Shield\nExperience: 875\n+100 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"This headdress will certainly be a wonderful gift for my brother.","done":"Thank you for your help, ‹name›.\nMy part in my brother's ceremony is almost complete. Giving him his headdress and witnessing the ceremony are all my duty requires of me.\nThunder Bluff Mulgore","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":37.8,"y":59.6,"n":"Eyahn Eagletalon","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["thunder-bluff"]},"264":{"id":264,"t":"Until Death Do Us Part","lv":15,"min":12,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Place Clarice's Pendant on Yuriv's Tomb in Silverpine.\nClarice's Pendant\nProvided: Clarice's Pendant","desc":"Filthy scum! Leaves me for his damn crusade. Because \"the Light is the most important thing we have against the threats the undead pose.\"\nWell, what about his children?! What about ME?! Night after night I sat patiently waiting for him... always second to his blasted duty!\nWell, witness what \"justice\" brings you, ‹name›! He's dead and I'm bearing the very thing he was trying to stop!\nTake this piece of junk and put it on his tomb at the Sepulcher. I want nothing to do with it anymore... or him!","rew":"Experience: 550","back":"The stone is cold to the touch, but has obviously been abused. Trash litters the area; nicks and gashes decorate the relief atop the coffin; and the foliage around the grave has started to grow over the site.\nNo one cares for whoever is buried here, especially not any victims of the plague.","done":"You place the worthless pendant on the grave, and the gemstone within the setting seems to dull noticeably.\nAs you stand to leave, you look down at the pendant; it lies lifelessly over the hands of the relief sculpted into the top of the coffin. Your thoughts are interrupted by a stiff, cool breeze passing over the Sepulcher. For a moment everything around you is silent.\nThunder Bluff Silverpine Forest","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":28.9,"y":26.4,"n":"Clarice Foster","s":1},{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":44.2,"y":42.7,"n":"Yuriv's Tombstone","e":1}],"cats":["thunder-bluff"]},"1064":{"id":1064,"t":"Forsaken Aid","lv":18,"min":13,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Apothecary Zamah in the Pools of Vision in Thunder Bluff.","desc":"The tauren have a bond with the land, and it pains me to hear of Stonetalon's plight. But I fear that to heal the land, we must first remove the disease upon it.\nIs it not fortunate, then, that the Forsaken are allied with us? They know much of disease. I believe they can aid us, and by doing so they will strengthen the trust between our people.\nSpeak with Apothecary Zamah. She is a scholar and an emissary of the Forsaken. You will find her in the Pools of Vision below the Spirit Rise.","rew":"Experience: 340\n+25 reputation with Thunder Bluff","done":"Magatha sent word of your coming, ‹name›. Although my heart beats no longer, I still feel sorrow for the spirits of Stonetalon.\nThe Forsaken are eager to offer what help we can.","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":69.9,"y":30.9,"n":"Magatha Grimtotem","s":1},{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":22.8,"y":20.9,"n":"Apothecary Zamah","e":1}],"cats":["thunder-bluff"]},"99144":{"id":99144,"t":"Seeking refuge","lv":7,"min":5,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Help Bareth Dawnstone escape Crusader's Outpost, and report his safety to Shari Stilwell in Brill.\nEscort Bareth Dawnstone out of Crusader's Outpost","desc":"Light bless you for finding me. I was on my way from Bandarion Keep to deliver a message to Shari Stilwell in Brill when these monsters captured me. They wield the Light with a hatred in their hearts that makes what's left of my blood seethe. It goes against all I meditate for... all I strive to protect!\n<Bareth Dawnstone steadies himself.>\nI know some still take issue with my kind, but I assure you our intentions are pure. If you would aid me in escaping this place, I would be forever grateful.","rew":"Money: 1 75 0 gold, 1 silver, 75 copper Experience: 625\n+100 reputation with Undercity","done":"Blessings upon you for aiding Dawnstone. Our order is still taking root here and it would be devastating to lose one so promising before his time.\nPlease accept this as a token of our thanks. Should you ever take an interest in our ways, our monastery Bandarion Keep lies on the bluffs northwest of the Solliden Farmstead. We welcome all who seek guidance in the Light.","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":32,"y":46.2,"n":"Bareth Dawnstone","s":1},{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":60.2,"y":52.6,"n":"Shari Stilwell","e":1}],"cats":["tirisfal-glades"]},"3784":{"id":3784,"t":"Assisting Arch Druid Runetotem","lv":50,"min":47,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem in Thunder Bluff.","desc":"Excuse me ‹class›, but I'd like just a moment of your time if possible.\nThe Cenarion Circle in Thunder Bluff is most interested in seasoned adventurers such as yourself to lend them aid in a vital research project. While I do not know the specifics, I can inform you that none other than Hamuul Runetotem is spearheading this research.\nPlease - if you are interested, speak with him directly on the Elder Rise within Thunder Bluff proper.","rew":"Experience: 470\n+10 reputation with Thunder Bluff","done":"Greetings, ‹class›; I am glad you are interested in assisting our research. There is much to do, and I would be doing you a disservice if I informed you that the work this entails is not dangerous. Hopefully this will not scare you off... but from the looks of you, I take it that danger is something that you have dealt with before.\nUndercity Thunder Bluff","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":67.7,"y":37.9,"n":"Innkeeper Norman","s":1},{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":78.6,"y":28.6,"n":"Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem","e":1}],"cats":["undercity"]},"7624":{"id":7624,"t":"Ulathek the Traitor","lv":58,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Confront Ulathek, then bring The Traitor's Heart to Lord Banehollow in Jaedenar.\nThe Traitor's Heart Ulathek","desc":"You wish to enter my good graces? Then kill for me.\nMy servant, Ulathek, is pathetic how he grovels before me, all the while plotting with Lord Hel'nurath on Xoroth. Hel'nurath plans to usurp my power here, and Ulathek is his spy...\nProve that you serve me and not my rivals. Confront Ulathek in his quarters, in the Shadow Hold to the west. Tell him that I know his secret and watch as fear grips him. Then, bring me the traitor's heart!","rew":"Experience: 6,200","back":"I can already taste the heart of Ulathek on my lips. So sweet is the flesh of a traitor...","done":"Ah, how splendid! After rotting a week, this heart will prove a succulent treat! Perhaps I will send for Ulathek's head and place it before me as I eat...\nYou have done me a service, warlock, and so my patience for you has grown. Marginally.","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":35.9,"y":44.4,"n":"Lord Banehollow","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"1704":{"id":1704,"t":"Klockmort Spannerspan","lv":28,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Furen's Notes to Klockmort Spannerspan.\nFuren's Notes\nProvided: Furen's Notes","desc":"I made a copy of my notes on the techniques I learned while making your armor, and need someone to take them to Klockmort Spannerspan. He's a gnomish blacksmith in Ironforge and when he learns what I've learned... I bet he'll pull off his own beard in excitement.","rew":"Experience: 575","back":"Good day, or morning or evening. I can't tell from way down here. So do you have business for me?","done":"Oh my! These notes are amazing! And what's more... they're incredible and they're stupendous and they make my knees go all a-wobbly!\nFuren had a breakthrough! A real breakthrough! I can't wait to try out his new technique!\nStormwind City Dun Morogh","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":64.6,"y":37.2,"n":"Furen Longbeard","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62,"y":28.5,"n":"Klockmort Spannerspan","e":1}],"cats":["warrior"]},"8424":{"id":8424,"t":"War on the Shadowsworn","lv":52,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Slaughter the Shadowsworn in the Blasted Lands and return to the Fallen Hero of the Horde.\nShadowsworn Adept slain : 0/ 20\nShadowsworn Cultist slain : 0/ 10\nShadowsworn Thug slain : 0/ 20","desc":"The continued presence of the shadowsworn in the Blasted Lands bring great pain to me. Their dark rituals and spells cause agony unlike any I felt while alive.\nThrough you I can deliver my own message of pain. Go forth and deliver my wrath.","rew":"Experience: 5,100","back":"The shadowsworn are not easily defeated, are they? But you are a warrior, and you will triumph or perish trying.","done":"Already you have subdued my pain and honored me. Thank you, warrior.\nSwamp of Sorrows Blasted Lands","pins":[{"z":"Swamp of Sorrows","x":34.3,"y":66.1,"n":"Fallen Hero of the Horde","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warrior"]},"4984":{"id":4984,"t":"The Wildlife Suffers Too","lv":54,"min":51,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Destroy 8 Diseased Wolves, and then return to Mulgris Deepriver at the Writhing Haunt, Western Plaguelands.\nDiseased Wolf slain : 0/ 8","desc":"While there was little I could do alone to thwart the Scourge, I nevertheless came to these lands to try and heal the damage done to nature. Animals suffer from the plague that continues to choke these lands, unable to find mercy and peace. I ask for you to continue what I could not finish here.\nThere is no salvation for the suffering animals but a sweet and merciful release. Seek out diseased wolves nearby and put them down. Please ‹name›, end their misery - doing so will surely soothe mine.","rew":"Experience: 4,100\n+75 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"The wolves that are infected with the plague must be put down, ‹name›. The disease they carry cannot be cured. I tried... I tried until I succumbed to the plague myself.","done":"I... I sense that the souls of those wolves you have put down now have rest. They - and I - thank you for a merciful release.\nThe wolves are not alone in their suffering within this damnable place, ‹name›. Please, I have need of you once more.","pins":[{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":53.7,"y":64.7,"n":"Mulgris Deepriver","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"5224":{"id":5224,"t":"Writhing Haunt Cauldron","lv":55,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Arcane Quickener sold by Alchemist Arbington , sold by Apothecary Dithers\n5 Somatic Intensifier Slavering Ghoul 50 % , Foulmane 50 % , Jabbering Ghoul 50 % , Blighted Zombie 50 % and 4 more\n4 Runecloth Stormwind Royal Guard , Honor Guard , Skullsplitter Speaker in Zul'Gurub , General Marcus Jonathan 85.7 % and 4 more","rew":"Experience: 550\n+25 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"The Scourge's plague cauldron stands before you, spewing vast amounts of toxins into the air. A small, non-descript access panel lies in the base of the cauldron's vast platform.\nHaving already defeated the cauldron lord and acquired its key, you are free to add the appropriate reagents to the cauldron to make a counter agent to the plague.","done":"Adding the reagents to the cauldron's mix begins to change the color and texture of the cloud it spews forth. Scourge that are even remotely near the cauldron appear to recoil at the introduction of the new components into the environment.","pins":[{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":53,"y":65.6,"n":"Scourge Cauldron","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"6184":{"id":6184,"t":"Flint Shadowmore","lv":60,"min":56,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to Chillwind Camp in the Western Plaguelands and meet up with your contact, Flint Shadowmore.","desc":"The only information we have thus far, then, is that Nathanos Marris may have been slain by this Blightcaller. We assume the Blightcaller is the same fiend that disposed of my agents.\nFlint Shadowmore, another SI:7 operative, is stationed at the Alliance encampment of Chillwind Point in the Western Plaguelands. Seek him out; he will debrief you on the current situation in the Plagues and give you an assignment.\nGood luck, ‹name›.","rew":"Experience: 4,950","done":"The first mission will be straight up, ‹name›. You go in, you come out. Recon...\nStormwind City Western Plaguelands","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":78.3,"y":70.7,"n":"Master Mathias Shaw","s":1},{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":43.6,"y":84.5,"n":"Flint Shadowmore","e":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"5944":{"id":5944,"t":"In Dreams","lv":60,"min":52,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 9,950 experience instead of 10,900, 0.91 times as much.","obj":"Escort Taelan Fordring out of Hearthglen.","desc":"For so long, I have been a puppet of the Grand Crusader. What reason was there to fight against what the Scarlet Crusade had become? It has been decades, yet the memories of my father; those precious memories, they are what have kept me alive.\nI have dreams, stranger. In these dreams my father is with me. He stands proudly at my side as I am inducted into the Order. We battle legion of Scourge, side by side. We bring honor to the Alliance, to Lordaeron.\nI want not to dream anymore.\nTake me to him.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nMark of Fordring Ornate Adamantium Breastplate Shimmering Platinum Warhammer Shroud of the Exile Fordring's Seal\nExperience: 9,950","back":"<Tirion regains his composure.>","done":"The death of my son at the hands of these monsters will not pass without incident. Take solace in knowing that the Order is reborn.\nI now take my place as Highlord of the new Order of the Silver Hand.\nThese possessions of my past - they are all that I have to offer for all that you have done. Please, take these as a symbol of my gratitude; all have served me well over the years.\nMay we meet again, in better times, and reminisce of days long past... battles hard fought... dreams redeemed.\nWestern Plaguelands Eastern Plaguelands","pins":[{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":42,"y":14.8,"n":"Highlord Taelan Fordring","s":1},{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":5.2,"y":35.6,"n":"Tirion Fordring","e":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"184":{"id":184,"t":"Furlbrow's Deed","lv":9,"min":8,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Furlbrow's Deed to Farmer Furlbrow.\nFurlbrow's Deed\nProvided: Furlbrow's Deed","desc":"This is the deed to an expanse of farmlands within Westfall. It is signed by a Theodore Furlbrow and cosigned by his wife, Verna. And on the back of the deed are hastily scrawled words:\n\"We leaned on Furlbrow and got his deed. Thought it might be handy if you wanted to forge one of these for your own place.\nThe Furlbrows won't give us trouble. Last I saw them they were on their way out of Westfall, stuck with a broken wagon.\"\nYou think the Furlbrows might want their deed back...","rew":"You will receive:\n5 Ripe Watermelon 5 Small Pumpkin\nExperience: 600\n+75 reputation with Stormwind","back":"You have the deed to my farm?? That's good news! Some ruffians stole it days ago... I thought it was gone for good!\nPlease, let me have it. We're on our way out of Westfall and ain't coming back any time soon, but if we do then we'll need those papers...","done":"Loads of thanks, ‹name›! As I was saying, these parts aren't fit for honest folk anymore, but if things get better, then this deed will let us reclaim our land.\nI don't have much to offer you, but here -- take this.","pins":[{"z":"Westfall","x":60,"y":19.4,"n":"Farmer Furlbrow","e":1}],"cats":["westfall"]},"92744":{"id":92744,"t":"Murloc gills","lv":12,"min":9,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Alba Fairmoon wants you to collect 7 Longshore Murloc Gills along the shoreline of Westfall.\n7 Longshore Murloc Gill","desc":"The corruption affecting Westfall's crops may have seeped into the ocean as well. If the local fish are affected too, it could doom Stormwind to famine.\nCollect gills from the murlocs along the shoreline and bring them to me. Murlocs are quite hardy, but their physiology is extremely sensitive to contaminants. Any toxins in the seawater will be readily apparent in the gills you find.","rew":"Money: 2 50 0 gold, 2 silver, 50 copper Experience: 460\n+50 reputation with Stormwind","back":"I hope the murlocs did not give you too much trouble?","done":"I see... these gills appear to be healthy, for now. But we must not be complacent.","pins":[{"z":"Westfall","x":52.4,"y":53,"n":"Alba Fairmoon","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["westfall"]},"104":{"id":104,"t":"The Coastal Menace","lv":20,"min":15,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring a scale of Old Murk-Eye to Captain Grayson at the Westfall Lighthouse.\nScale of Old Murk-Eye Old Murk-Eye","desc":"When my life was ended upon the rocks, I had no clue what the afterlife held for me. The Lighthouse was black that night because Old Murk-Eye had scared the keeper's family off. They returned and re-lit the flame but Old Murk-Eye coerced the weaker minded murlocs to raid the Lighthouse with him once again. The second time the family was not so lucky and before my eyes they perished helplessly.\nSlay Old Murk-Eye if you see him along the shore and bring me one of his scales and I shall reward you.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nGrayson's Torch Buckler of the Seas Torchlight Wand\nExperience: 1,550","back":"Have you laid waste to the menace known as Old Murk-Eye yet? He has been spotted roaming the coastline of Westfall.\nReturn to me when the foul beast is dead.","done":"So the foul heathen, Murk-Eye is dead. Well done, ‹name›. By your hands one life was laid to rest but perhaps many more were saved. The Great Sea, wrought with danger as it is, shall be a wee bit safer this night thanks to your heroics.","pins":[{"z":"Westfall","x":30,"y":86,"n":"Captain Grayson","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["westfall"]},"8184":{"id":8184,"t":"Presence of Might","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring me thise things and I will create a powerful enchantment for you!\nPrimal Hakkari Idol\nPunctured Voodoo Doll\nPrimal Hakkari Idol Jin'do the Hexxer in Zul'Gurub , Bloodlord Mandokir in Zul'Gurub\nPunctured Voodoo Doll Zulian Cub 0.1 % in Zul'Gurub , Hakkari Shadowcaster 0 % in Zul'Gurub , Zulian Tiger 0 % in Zul'Gurub , Gurubashi Axe Thrower 0 % in Zul'Gurub and 4 more","desc":"Zanza can create the ancient troll enchantments with the right components.\nThe first is a primal Hakkari idol that must be taken from the most powerful of the Hakkari lieutenants: Jin'do and the Bloodlord.\nThe second is a punctured voodoo doll. These can be found in the piles of refuse that litter\nthis foul place. Look inside the jinxed hoodoo. Bring me these things and I will create a powerful enchantment for you!","rew":"You will receive:\nPresence of Might\n+100 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","back":"Bring me these things and I will create a powerful enchantment for you!","done":"Use it well, ‹class›. Show the Hakkari no mercy!\nStart Zanza the Restless Zul'Gurub End Zanza the Restless Zul'Gurub Level 60 , requires level 58 Difficulty 58 Side Human, Orc, Dwarf, Night Elf, Undead, Tauren, Gnome, Troll Type Raid Shareable No Repeatable Yes Quest ID 8184","cats":["zulgurub"]},"8104":{"id":8104,"t":"The Jewel of Kajaro","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 58 instead of 60.","obj":"Pebble of Kajaro","rew":"You will receive:\nJewel of Kajaro\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","back":"Give me the talisman, ‹name›. I must show you something.","done":"<Al'tabim shatters the pebble with a powerful unseen force.>\nDo you see? The pebble is what we call a geode. Inside the pebble are powerful crystals that have been soaking in the latent energies from our world. By cutting the pebble in half, I have finally allowed its full potential to be realized. Use it to lay waste to our enemies.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":15.3,"y":16.1,"n":"Al'tabim the All-Seeing","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zulgurub"]}});